    deepExplanation: "Example:\n\n```ts\nconst start = performance.now();\n\n// Keep expensive work bounded and measurable.\nconst result = Array.from({ length: 10_000 }, (_, i) => i * 2);\n\nconsole.log(result.length);\nconsole.log(`elapsed ≈ ${(performance.now() - start).toFixed(2)}ms`);\n```\n\nProduction pattern:\n\n```ts\n// Measure before and after an optimization instead of assuming it helps.\nperformance.mark(\"work-start\");\n// ...operation...\nperformance.mark(\"work-end\");\nperformance.measure(\"work\", \"work-start\", \"work-end\");\n\nconsole.table(performance.getEntriesByName(\"work\").map(({ duration }) => ({\n  durationMs: Number(duration.toFixed(2)),\n})));\n```\n\nWhy it matters: Directly affects user experience and conversion-sensitive flows. Performance regressions accumulate through dependencies, features and third-party code. Enterprise teams need budgets, ownership and observability—not one-time optimization.",
